  "statement": "Wherever the matrix holds a zero, set that entire row and column to zero. Do it in place; nothing is returned.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= rows, cols <= 200"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Zeroing as you find each zero is wrong: the zeros you write get read as originals and cascade.",
    "So do two passes. First record which rows and columns must be cleared, then clear them.",
    "For O(1) space, store those flags in the matrix first row and first column, handling those two lines separately at the end."
  ],
